@startuml
title Scenario Creation - Current Architecture
caption Before introducing a Factory Method abstraction

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam linetype ortho

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
}

package "HTTP and Session Layer" {

  class ApiServer <<HTTP Controller>>

  class JsonMapper <<JSON Mapping>>

  class SessionStore <<Session Management>>
}

package "Simulation Domain" {

  class SimulationEngine <<Facade>>

  class Scenario <<Domain Model>>

  class Process

  class Resource
}

ApiServer --> JsonMapper : parse configuration data

ApiServer --> SessionStore : resolve browser session

SessionStore --> SimulationEngine : provide session engine

ApiServer ..> SimulationEngine : configure scenario

SimulationEngine --> Scenario : maintain active scenario

Scenario *-- Process : contains

Scenario *-- Resource : contains

note bottom of ApiServer
  Receives scenario configuration
  through the HTTP API.

  Validates the request before
  applying the configuration.
end note

note bottom of SimulationEngine
  Coordinates scenario configuration
  and subsequent simulation actions.

  No interchangeable scenario
  creation factories are required.
end note

note bottom of Scenario
  Contains the configured
  processes and resource types.

  Configuration includes operations,
  avoidance and prevention settings.
end note

legend bottom
  Current architecture at a conceptual level.

  No dedicated Factory Method hierarchy
  is represented in the implemented design.

  Exact Java method signatures are omitted.
endlegend

@enduml
